IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nsw-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales), Part 4 Amendments and repeals: sections 27 to 30D.
-- The moment a repeal takes effect (section 30D) and the day an amending Act is repealed (section 30C(2) and (3)) are computed in nsw-interpretation-time.l4.

§ `Part 4 Amendments and repeals`

§§ `27 Acts may be amended etc in the same session of Parliament`

-- src:265 | An Act may be amended or repealed in the same session of Parliament as that in which it was passed.
@ref s 27 (src:265)
GIVEN `the amendment or repeal is made in the same session of Parliament as that in which the Act was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27 an Act may be amended or repealed` MEANS
    IF `the amendment or repeal is made in the same session of Parliament as that in which the Act was passed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `28 Repealed Acts and statutory rules not revived`

-- src:268 | An Act or statutory rule that has been repealed by some other Act or statutory rule is not revived merely because the other Act or statutory rule is subsequently amended or repealed or subsequently ceases to have effect.
@ref s 28 (src:268)
GIVEN `the Act or statutory rule has been repealed by some other Act or statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other Act or statutory rule is subsequently amended or repealed or subsequently ceases to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28 the repealed Act or statutory rule is revived merely because the repealing Act or statutory rule is subsequently amended or repealed or ceases to have effect` MEANS
    IF `the Act or statutory rule has been repealed by some other Act or statutory rule` AND `the other Act or statutory rule is subsequently amended or repealed or subsequently ceases to have effect`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `29 Repealed Acts and statutory rules continue in force`

-- Fork: the repealed provisions continue in force "until the new provisions commence".
-- The new provisions commence at the beginning of their commencement day (section 24), so the repealed provisions are in force on every day before that day and not on it.
-- src:271 | If an Act or statutory rule repeals some or all of the provisions of some other Act or statutory rule and enacts new provisions in substitution for the repealed provisions, the repealed provisions continue in force until the new provisions commence.
@ref s 29 (src:271)
GIVEN `the Act or statutory rule repeals some or all of the provisions of some other Act or statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it enacts new provisions in substitution for the repealed provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the new provisions commence` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29 the repealed provisions are in force on the day` MEANS
    IF `the Act or statutory rule repeals some or all of the provisions of some other Act or statutory rule` AND `it enacts new provisions in substitution for the repealed provisions`
    THEN JUST (Day `the day asked about` LESS THAN Day `the day the new provisions commence`)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `29A Revocation of repeal of Acts and instruments`

-- src:274 | (1) The Governor may, by proclamation published on the NSW legislation website, revoke the repeal of an Act or instrument if the revocation of the repeal is authorised by this section. In that case, the Act or instrument is taken not to be, and never to have been, repealed.
@ref s 29A(1) revocation by proclamation (src:274)
GIVEN `the revocation of the repeal is authorised by section 29A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the revocation is by proclamation published on the NSW legislation website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29A(1) the Governor may revoke the repeal of an Act or instrument` MEANS
    IF NOT `the revocation of the repeal is authorised by section 29A`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the revocation is by proclamation published on the NSW legislation website`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- src:274 | (1) The Governor may, by proclamation published on the NSW legislation website, revoke the repeal of an Act or instrument if the revocation of the repeal is authorised by this section. In that case, the Act or instrument is taken not to be, and never to have been, repealed.
@ref s 29A(1) effect of revocation (src:274)
GIVEN `the repeal has been revoked under section 29A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29A(1) the Act or instrument is taken not to be, and never to have been, repealed` MEANS
    IF `the repeal has been revoked under section 29A` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:275 | (2) The revocation of the repeal of an Act or instrument is authorised only if, at the time of the repeal, the Act or instrument effecting the repeal—
-- src:276 | (a) stated that this section applied to the repeal or otherwise authorised the Governor to revoke the repeal, or
-- src:277 | (b) described the repeal (in a heading or otherwise) as the repeal of redundant, spent or unnecessary Acts or instruments.
@ref s 29A(2) (src:275-277)
GIVEN `at the time of the repeal the repealing Act or instrument stated that section 29A applied to the repeal or otherwise authorised the Governor to revoke the repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the repeal the repealing Act or instrument described the repeal as the repeal of redundant, spent or unnecessary Acts or instruments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29A(2) the revocation of the repeal of an Act or instrument is authorised` MEANS
    `at the time of the repeal the repealing Act or instrument stated that section 29A applied to the repeal or otherwise authorised the Governor to revoke the repeal`
    OR `at the time of the repeal the repealing Act or instrument described the repeal as the repeal of redundant, spent or unnecessary Acts or instruments`

-- src:278 | (3) The revocation of the repeal of an Act or instrument under this section does not operate so as—
-- src:279 | (a) to affect in a manner prejudicial to any person (other than the State or an authority of the State) the rights of that person existing before the revocation of the repeal, or
@ref s 29A(3)(a) (src:278-279)
GIVEN `the person is the State or an authority of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rights of the person existing before the revocation of the repeal are affected in a manner prejudicial to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29A(3)(a) the revocation of the repeal operates so as to affect the rights of the person` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is the State or an authority of the State`) AND `the rights of the person existing before the revocation of the repeal are affected in a manner prejudicial to the person`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:278 | (3) The revocation of the repeal of an Act or instrument under this section does not operate so as—
-- src:279 | (a) to affect in a manner prejudicial to any person (other than the State or an authority of the State) the rights of that person existing before the revocation of the repeal, or
-- src:280 | (b) to impose liabilities on any person (other than the State or an authority of the State) in respect of anything done or omitted to be done before the revocation of the repeal.
@ref s 29A(3)(b) (src:278-280)
GIVEN `the person is the State or an authority of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `liabilities would be imposed on the person in respect of anything done or omitted to be done before the revocation of the repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29A(3)(b) the revocation of the repeal operates so as to impose liabilities on the person` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is the State or an authority of the State`) AND `liabilities would be imposed on the person in respect of anything done or omitted to be done before the revocation of the repeal`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `30 Effect of amendment or repeal of Acts and statutory rules`

-- What subsections (1) and (2) say is not affected. Subsection (2) opens "Without limiting the effect of subsection (1)", so the list is not closed.
DECLARE ThingNotAffectedByAmendmentOrRepeal IS ONE OF
    ARevivalOfAnythingNotInForceOrExisting
    ThePreviousOperationOrAnythingDulyDone
    ARightPrivilegeObligationOrLiabilityAcquiredAccruedOrIncurred
    APenaltyIncurredForAnOffence
    AnInvestigationLegalProceedingOrRemedy
    TheProofOfAPastActOrThing
    ARightPrivilegeObligationOrLiabilityPreservedByTheAct
    AnAmendmentOrValidationMadeByTheAct
    ASavingsOrTransitionalProvision
    AnotherThing

-- src:283 | (1) The amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule does not—
-- src:284 | (a) revive anything not in force or existing at the time at which the amendment or repeal takes effect, or
-- src:285 | (b) affect the previous operation of the Act or statutory rule or anything duly suffered, done or commenced under the Act or statutory rule, or
-- src:286 | (c) affect any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the Act or statutory rule, or
-- src:287 | (d) affect any penalty incurred in respect of any offence arising under the Act or statutory rule, or
-- src:288 | (e) affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of any such right, privilege, obligation, liability or penalty,
-- src:289 | and any such penalty may be imposed and enforced, and any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, as if the Act or statutory rule had not been amended or repealed.
-- src:290 | (2) Without limiting the effect of subsection (1), the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule does not affect—
-- src:291 | (a) the proof of any past act or thing, or
-- src:292 | (b) any right, privilege, obligation or liability saved by the operation of the Act or statutory rule, or
-- src:293 | (c) any amendment or validation made by the Act or statutory rule, or
-- src:294 | (d) the operation of any savings or transitional provision contained in the Act or statutory rule.
@ref s 30(1) and (2) (src:283-294)
GIVEN thing IS A ThingNotAffectedByAmendmentOrRepeal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(1) and (2) the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule affects the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN ARevivalOfAnythingNotInForceOrExisting THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN ThePreviousOperationOrAnythingDulyDone THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN ARightPrivilegeObligationOrLiabilityAcquiredAccruedOrIncurred THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN APenaltyIncurredForAnOffence THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN AnInvestigationLegalProceedingOrRemedy THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN TheProofOfAPastActOrThing THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN ARightPrivilegeObligationOrLiabilityPreservedByTheAct THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN AnAmendmentOrValidationMadeByTheAct THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN ASavingsOrTransitionalProvision THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN AnotherThing THEN NOTHING

-- src:289 | and any such penalty may be imposed and enforced, and any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, as if the Act or statutory rule had not been amended or repealed.
@ref s 30(1) closing words (src:289)
GIVEN thing IS A ThingNotAffectedByAmendmentOrRepeal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(1) the penalty may be imposed and enforced, or the investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, as if the Act or statutory rule had not been amended or repealed` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN APenaltyIncurredForAnOffence THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AnInvestigationLegalProceedingOrRemedy THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN ARevivalOfAnythingNotInForceOrExisting THEN NOTHING
    WHEN ThePreviousOperationOrAnythingDulyDone THEN NOTHING
    WHEN ARightPrivilegeObligationOrLiabilityAcquiredAccruedOrIncurred THEN NOTHING
    WHEN TheProofOfAPastActOrThing THEN NOTHING
    WHEN ARightPrivilegeObligationOrLiabilityPreservedByTheAct THEN NOTHING
    WHEN AnAmendmentOrValidationMadeByTheAct THEN NOTHING
    WHEN ASavingsOrTransitionalProvision THEN NOTHING
    WHEN AnotherThing THEN NOTHING

-- src:295 | (3) This section applies to the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule in addition to, and without limiting the effect of, any provision of the Act or statutory rule by which the amendment or repeal is effected.
@ref s 30(3) (src:295)
GIVEN `it is the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(3) section 30 applies to the amendment or repeal in addition to any provision of the Act or statutory rule by which it is effected` MEANS
    IF `it is the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- What subsection (4) says counts as an amendment or repeal. "includes" does not close the list.
DECLARE EventCountedAsAmendmentOrRepeal IS ONE OF
    TheExpirationOfTheActOrStatutoryRule
    AnAmendmentOrRepealEffectedByImplication
    TheAbrogationLimitationOrExtensionOfTheEffectOfTheActOrStatutoryRule
    TheExclusionFromTheApplicationOfTheActOrStatutoryRule
    TheInclusionWithinTheApplicationOfTheActOrStatutoryRule
    AnotherEvent

-- src:296 | (4) In this section, a reference to the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule includes—
-- src:297 | (a) a reference to the expiration of the Act or statutory rule,
-- src:298 | (b) a reference to an amendment or repeal of the Act or statutory rule effected by implication,
-- src:299 | (c) a reference to the abrogation, limitation or extension of the effect of the Act or statutory rule, and
-- src:300 | (d) a reference to—
-- src:301 | (i) the exclusion from the application of the Act or statutory rule, or
-- src:302 | (ii) the inclusion within the application of the Act or statutory rule,
-- src:303 | of any person, subject-matter or circumstance.
@ref s 30(4) (src:296-303)
GIVEN event IS A EventCountedAsAmendmentOrRepeal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(4) the event is a reference to the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule in section 30` MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN TheExpirationOfTheActOrStatutoryRule THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AnAmendmentOrRepealEffectedByImplication THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheAbrogationLimitationOrExtensionOfTheEffectOfTheActOrStatutoryRule THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheExclusionFromTheApplicationOfTheActOrStatutoryRule THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheInclusionWithinTheApplicationOfTheActOrStatutoryRule THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AnotherEvent THEN NOTHING

§§ `30A Transferred provisions`

-- src:306 | (1) This section applies where a provision is transferred from an Act or statutory rule to another Act or statutory rule and an Act or statutory rule states that the provision is a transferred provision to which this section applies.
@ref s 30A(1) (src:306)
GIVEN `a provision is transferred from an Act or statutory rule to another Act or statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an Act or statutory rule states that the provision is a transferred provision to which section 30A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30A(1) section 30A applies to the provision` MEANS
    IF `a provision is transferred from an Act or statutory rule to another Act or statutory rule` AND `an Act or statutory rule states that the provision is a transferred provision to which section 30A applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:307 | (2) The transfer does not affect the operation (if any) or meaning of the provision, and accordingly the provision is to be construed as if it had not been so transferred.
@ref s 30A(2) (src:307)
GIVEN `section 30A applies to the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30A(2) the provision is construed as if it had not been transferred` MEANS
    IF `section 30A applies to the provision` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:308 | (3) This section applies whether or not the provision is modified, but has effect subject to any such modification.
@ref s 30A(3) (src:308)
GIVEN `section 30A applies to the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is modified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30A(3) section 30A applies whether or not the provision is modified` MEANS
    IF `section 30A applies to the provision` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `30B Effect of amendment of instrument by an Act`

-- src:311 | The amendment of an instrument by an Act does not prevent its later amendment or repeal by another instrument.
@ref s 30B (src:311)
GIVEN `the instrument has been amended by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30B the amendment of the instrument by an Act prevents its later amendment or repeal by another instrument` MEANS
    IF `the instrument has been amended by an Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `30C Automatic repeal of amending Acts that have commenced`

-- Where in an Act the text sits. Paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition of "amending Act" name five places.
DECLARE PlaceInAnAct IS ONE OF
    AWholeAct
    ASectionOrSubsectionOfAnAct
    AScheduleOrSubscheduleToAnAct
    AProvisionOfAScheduleOrSubschedule
    AnotherPlaceInAnAct

-- src:315 | amending Act means—
-- src:316 | (a) a whole Act that directly amends or repeals other Acts or instruments and that contains no other provisions apart from ancillary provisions, or
-- src:317 | (b) a section or subsection of an Act, a schedule or subschedule to an Act or a provision of any such schedule or subschedule that directly amends or repeals other Acts or instruments and that contains no other provisions apart from ancillary provisions.
@ref s 30C(1) amending Act (src:315-317)
GIVEN place IS A PlaceInAnAct
      `it directly amends or repeals other Acts or instruments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contains no other provisions apart from ancillary provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30C(1) the text is an amending Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN AWholeAct THEN `it directly amends or repeals other Acts or instruments` AND `it contains no other provisions apart from ancillary provisions`
    WHEN ASectionOrSubsectionOfAnAct THEN `it directly amends or repeals other Acts or instruments` AND `it contains no other provisions apart from ancillary provisions`
    WHEN AScheduleOrSubscheduleToAnAct THEN `it directly amends or repeals other Acts or instruments` AND `it contains no other provisions apart from ancillary provisions`
    WHEN AProvisionOfAScheduleOrSubschedule THEN `it directly amends or repeals other Acts or instruments` AND `it contains no other provisions apart from ancillary provisions`
    WHEN AnotherPlaceInAnAct THEN FALSE

-- The six things the definition of "ancillary provision" lists.
DECLARE KindOfProvision IS ONE OF
    TheLongTitle
    APreamble
    AProvisionSpecifyingTheShortTitleOrName
    AProvisionProvidingForCommencement
    AProvisionDeclaringThatNotesDoNotFormPartOfTheAct
    AProvisionGivingEffectToOrDescribingASchedule
    AnotherKindOfProvision

-- src:318 | ancillary provision of an amending Act means the long title of the Act, a preamble to the Act, a provision that specifies the short title or name of the Act, a provision that provides for the commencement of the Act, a provision that declares that notes in the Act do not form part of the Act or a provision that gives effect to or describes a schedule to the Act.
@ref s 30C(1) ancillary provision (src:318)
GIVEN kind IS A KindOfProvision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30C(1) the provision is an ancillary provision of an amending Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN TheLongTitle THEN TRUE
    WHEN APreamble THEN TRUE
    WHEN AProvisionSpecifyingTheShortTitleOrName THEN TRUE
    WHEN AProvisionProvidingForCommencement THEN TRUE
    WHEN AProvisionDeclaringThatNotesDoNotFormPartOfTheAct THEN TRUE
    WHEN AProvisionGivingEffectToOrDescribingASchedule THEN TRUE
    WHEN AnotherKindOfProvision THEN FALSE

-- src:321 | (4) The repeal by this section of an amending Act does not, because of the operation of section 30, affect any amendment or repeal made by the amending Act.
@ref s 30C(4) (src:321)
GIVEN `the amending Act is repealed by section 30C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30C(4) the repeal by section 30C of an amending Act affects an amendment or repeal made by the amending Act` MEANS
    IF `the amending Act is repealed by section 30C` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:322 | (5) This section does not apply to an amending Act that makes provision for the repeal of the amending Act.
-- src:323 | (6) This section applies only to an amending Act enacted after 1 January 2009.
@ref s 30C(5) and (6) (src:322-323)
GIVEN `the date of assent to the amending Act` IS A DATE
      `the amending Act makes provision for the repeal of the amending Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30C(5) and (6) section 30C applies to the amending Act` MEANS
    (NOT `the amending Act makes provision for the repeal of the amending Act`) AND `s 30C(6) the amending Act was enacted after 1 January 2009` `the date of assent to the amending Act`

-- The day section 30C repeals the amending Act, when section 30C applies to it. When it does not apply, the section says nothing about the day.
-- src:319 | (2) An amending Act is repealed on the day after all of its provisions have commenced (except as provided by subsection (3)).
-- src:320 | (3) If an amending Act commences before the date of assent, the amending Act is repealed on the day after the date of assent.
@ref s 30C(2) and (3) the day of the repeal (src:319-320)
GIVEN `the date of assent to the amending Act` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which a provision of the amending Act commences` IS A DATE
      `the amending Act makes provision for the repeal of the amending Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 30C the day section 30C repeals the amending Act` MEANS
    IF `s 30C(5) and (6) section 30C applies to the amending Act` `the date of assent to the amending Act` `the amending Act makes provision for the repeal of the amending Act`
    THEN JUST (`s 30C(2) and (3) the day an amending Act is repealed` `the date of assent to the amending Act` `the last day on which a provision of the amending Act commences`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `30D Time of repeal of Acts and instruments`

-- Section 30D is computed in nsw-interpretation-time.l4 as `s 30D the moment a repeal on a day takes effect`.

§§ `Tests: Part 4`

-- s 27
#ASSERT `s 27 an Act may be amended or repealed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27 an Act may be amended or repealed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 28
#ASSERT `s 28 the repealed Act or statutory rule is revived merely because the repealing Act or statutory rule is subsequently amended or repealed or ceases to have effect` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28 the repealed Act or statutory rule is revived merely because the repealing Act or statutory rule is subsequently amended or repealed or ceases to have effect` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28 the repealed Act or statutory rule is revived merely because the repealing Act or statutory rule is subsequently amended or repealed or ceases to have effect` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 29: the new provisions commence on 1 July 2026, at the beginning of that day
#ASSERT `s 29 the repealed provisions are in force on the day` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29 the repealed provisions are in force on the day` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29 the repealed provisions are in force on the day` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 2 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29 the repealed provisions are in force on the day` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29 the repealed provisions are in force on the day` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 29A(1)
#ASSERT `s 29A(1) the Governor may revoke the repeal of an Act or instrument` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29A(1) the Governor may revoke the repeal of an Act or instrument` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29A(1) the Governor may revoke the repeal of an Act or instrument` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29A(1) the Act or instrument is taken not to be, and never to have been, repealed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29A(1) the Act or instrument is taken not to be, and never to have been, repealed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 29A(2): "only if" one of two things was done at the time of the repeal
#ASSERT `s 29A(2) the revocation of the repeal of an Act or instrument is authorised` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29A(2) the revocation of the repeal of an Act or instrument is authorised` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29A(2) the revocation of the repeal of an Act or instrument is authorised` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29A(2) the revocation of the repeal of an Act or instrument is authorised` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 29A(3): a person other than the State or an authority of the State
#ASSERT `s 29A(3)(a) the revocation of the repeal operates so as to affect the rights of the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29A(3)(a) the revocation of the repeal operates so as to affect the rights of the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29A(3)(a) the revocation of the repeal operates so as to affect the rights of the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29A(3)(b) the revocation of the repeal operates so as to impose liabilities on the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29A(3)(b) the revocation of the repeal operates so as to impose liabilities on the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29A(3)(b) the revocation of the repeal operates so as to impose liabilities on the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 30: the listed things, and one that is not listed
#ASSERT `s 30(1) and (2) the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule affects the thing` ARevivalOfAnythingNotInForceOrExisting EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30(1) and (2) the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule affects the thing` ThePreviousOperationOrAnythingDulyDone EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30(1) and (2) the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule affects the thing` ARightPrivilegeObligationOrLiabilityAcquiredAccruedOrIncurred EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30(1) and (2) the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule affects the thing` APenaltyIncurredForAnOffence EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30(1) and (2) the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule affects the thing` AnInvestigationLegalProceedingOrRemedy EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30(1) and (2) the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule affects the thing` TheProofOfAPastActOrThing EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30(1) and (2) the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule affects the thing` ARightPrivilegeObligationOrLiabilityPreservedByTheAct EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30(1) and (2) the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule affects the thing` AnAmendmentOrValidationMadeByTheAct EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30(1) and (2) the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule affects the thing` ASavingsOrTransitionalProvision EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30(1) and (2) the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule affects the thing` AnotherThing EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 30(1) the penalty may be imposed and enforced, or the investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, as if the Act or statutory rule had not been amended or repealed` APenaltyIncurredForAnOffence EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(1) the penalty may be imposed and enforced, or the investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, as if the Act or statutory rule had not been amended or repealed` AnInvestigationLegalProceedingOrRemedy EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(1) the penalty may be imposed and enforced, or the investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, as if the Act or statutory rule had not been amended or repealed` TheProofOfAPastActOrThing EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 30(3)
#ASSERT `s 30(3) section 30 applies to the amendment or repeal in addition to any provision of the Act or statutory rule by which it is effected` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(3) section 30 applies to the amendment or repeal in addition to any provision of the Act or statutory rule by which it is effected` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 30(4)
#ASSERT `s 30(4) the event is a reference to the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule in section 30` TheExpirationOfTheActOrStatutoryRule EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(4) the event is a reference to the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule in section 30` AnAmendmentOrRepealEffectedByImplication EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(4) the event is a reference to the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule in section 30` TheAbrogationLimitationOrExtensionOfTheEffectOfTheActOrStatutoryRule EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(4) the event is a reference to the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule in section 30` TheExclusionFromTheApplicationOfTheActOrStatutoryRule EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(4) the event is a reference to the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule in section 30` TheInclusionWithinTheApplicationOfTheActOrStatutoryRule EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(4) the event is a reference to the amendment or repeal of an Act or statutory rule in section 30` AnotherEvent EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 30A
#ASSERT `s 30A(1) section 30A applies to the provision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30A(1) section 30A applies to the provision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30A(1) section 30A applies to the provision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30A(2) the provision is construed as if it had not been transferred` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30A(2) the provision is construed as if it had not been transferred` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 30A(3) section 30A applies whether or not the provision is modified` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30A(3) section 30A applies whether or not the provision is modified` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30A(3) section 30A applies whether or not the provision is modified` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 30B
#ASSERT `s 30B the amendment of the instrument by an Act prevents its later amendment or repeal by another instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30B the amendment of the instrument by an Act prevents its later amendment or repeal by another instrument` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 30C(1): "means", so a closed definition
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the text is an amending Act` AWholeAct TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the text is an amending Act` AWholeAct TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the text is an amending Act` AWholeAct FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the text is an amending Act` ASectionOrSubsectionOfAnAct TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the text is an amending Act` AScheduleOrSubscheduleToAnAct TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the text is an amending Act` AProvisionOfAScheduleOrSubschedule TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the text is an amending Act` AnotherPlaceInAnAct TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the provision is an ancillary provision of an amending Act` TheLongTitle EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the provision is an ancillary provision of an amending Act` APreamble EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the provision is an ancillary provision of an amending Act` AProvisionSpecifyingTheShortTitleOrName EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the provision is an ancillary provision of an amending Act` AProvisionProvidingForCommencement EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the provision is an ancillary provision of an amending Act` AProvisionDeclaringThatNotesDoNotFormPartOfTheAct EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the provision is an ancillary provision of an amending Act` AProvisionGivingEffectToOrDescribingASchedule EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(1) the provision is an ancillary provision of an amending Act` AnotherKindOfProvision EQUALS FALSE
-- s 30C(4)
#ASSERT `s 30C(4) the repeal by section 30C of an amending Act affects an amendment or repeal made by the amending Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30C(4) the repeal by section 30C of an amending Act affects an amendment or repeal made by the amending Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 30C(5) and (6): enacted after 1 January 2009, and no provision for its own repeal
#ASSERT `s 30C(5) and (6) section 30C applies to the amending Act` (Date 2 1 2009) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30C(5) and (6) section 30C applies to the amending Act` (Date 1 1 2009) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30C(5) and (6) section 30C applies to the amending Act` (Date 31 12 2008) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30C(5) and (6) section 30C applies to the amending Act` (Date 2 1 2009) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 30C(2) and (3): assent 1 March 2020
#ASSERT `s 30C the day section 30C repeals the amending Act` (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 10 3 2020) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2020)
#ASSERT `s 30C the day section 30C repeals the amending Act` (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 3 2020) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2020)
#ASSERT `s 30C the day section 30C repeals the amending Act` (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 2 2020) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2020)
#ASSERT `s 30C the day section 30C repeals the amending Act` (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 10 3 2020) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 30C the day section 30C repeals the amending Act` (Date 1 3 2008) (Date 10 3 2008) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
